From 183c265f70638660ac3f0df86791fd4d50694062 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 110/168] pmdomain: mediatek: mtk-mfg: Add MT6858 support

The MT6858 speaks the MT8196's GPU-DVFS IPI protocol, but differs in
three ways:

- The bootloader starts the EB, and the EB stays on: the vendor kernel
  runs without GHPM and never powers it on or off. So there is no EB
  power sequence and no sleep channel. The IPI magic is read once, at
  probe, after checking in the SPM that MFG0 (the EB's domain) is on;
  without that check, a missing EB would hang the bus.
- Its firmware's shared status has two more words after the activity
  counter and different tables before the OPP tables. Move the offsets
  that the driver uses into a per-variant layout. The MT6858 offsets
  come from the vendor gpufreq wrapper that matches this firmware.
- It has a single buck, and the vendor kernel sets OPPs with CMD_COMMIT
  on the GPU target, which also keeps the EB's own thermal and battery
  limits in force. Do the same.

Since an always-on EB answers at once, give it its shared memory before
the first power request, as the vendor driver does. After a power-on,
check that the EB counted the GPU MTCMOS on before letting the GPU
driver at its registers.
---
 drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-mfg-pmdomain.c | 218 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 187 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-mfg-pmdomain.c b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mtk-mfg-pmdomain.c
index 093f8fac2..0f5896796 100644
